well on this christmas day catholic  charities offered a christmas meal to  hundreds  as 8 news now reporter kate houston  tells us it's bringing hope and comfort  to those who need it most nearly 1 000  men and women will be served a christmas  meal today  catholic charities says that the need  this year is unlike any other  today staff is serving the homeless and  those on the brink of homelessness  their plates were filled with prime rib  vegetables and cake  catholic charities says this may be the  first nice meal they've had all year  due to the pandemic deacon tom roberts  says this year has been unique and  challenging  while the need in the community has  always been there he says  it feels different there's a bit more  desperation  a bit more anxiety a bit more tension  this year because so many people have  never been in this situation before  find themselves in these difficult  circumstances people like keith zorros  who's been homeless for a few months  i've been looking for work for months  you know  no nobody's hiring and it's very hard  to find a way back home  zoros tells me despite the challenges  he's facing  he's grateful for what he has i am  blessed  to have food on my plate because there  are brothers and sisters out there that  have no food on their plate  that don't come into these  establishments and  actually acquiesce to being given  gifts this is the 55th year catholic  charities has served a christmas meal to  the community  while there were no volunteers this year  staff was on hand to make sure everyone  followed health and safety guidelines  kate houston 8 news now and catholic  charities developed a special holiday  menu for today and  it was all free
 

